# Question 8 — Shallow Copy vs Reference Assignment

These are completely different:

### Reference assignment

```javascript
const admin = user;
```

No new object is created.

```javascript
admin === user
// true
```

### Shallow copy

```javascript
const admin = { ...user };
```

A new outer object is created.

```javascript
admin === user
// false
```

But nested objects can still share references.

