# Question 14 — Symbols

### Code

```javascript
const id = Symbol("id");

const user = {
    name: "Rahul",
    age: 25,
    [id]: 101
};
```

The Symbol property is still an **own property**.

You can access it with:

```javascript
user[id]
```

which returns:

```text
101
```

But:

```javascript
Object.keys(user)
```

doesn't include Symbol properties.

To retrieve Symbol keys:

```javascript
Object.getOwnPropertySymbols(user);
```

### Production concept

Symbols provide unique property keys and can be useful when you want to avoid accidental property-name collisions.

