# Question 15 — Nested State Update

### Original object

```javascript
const state = {
    user: {
        name: "Rahul",
        address: {
            city: "Ahmedabad",
            pincode: 380001
        }
    },
    cart: [
        {
            id: 1,
            name: "Laptop",
            quantity: 1
        }
    ]
};
```

### Direct mutation

```javascript
state.user.address.city = "Mumbai";
```

This directly modifies the original object.

### Immutable update

```javascript
const newState = {
    ...state,
    user: {
        ...state.user,
        address: {
            ...state.user.address,
            city: "Mumbai"
        }
    }
};
```

Now:

```javascript
newState !== state
newState.user !== state.user
newState.user.address !== state.user.address
```

while unchanged portions can continue to share references.

This idea is called **structural sharing**.

