# 25. Arrow Function + `this`

You also correctly identified:

> Arrow functions don't have their own `this`; they use lexical `this`.

Therefore:

```js
const user = {
    name: "Bhavya",

    greet: () => {
        console.log(this.name);
    }
};
```

doesn't make `this` refer to `user`.

For object methods that need the calling object's `this`, use:

```js
greet() {}
```

rather than an arrow function.

