# 31. `||` vs `??`

One of the **most important interview questions**.

```js
const value = 0;

console.log(value || 100);
console.log(value ?? 100);
```

Output:

```text
100
0
```

Why?

`||` checks **truthiness**.

`??` checks only **null/undefined**.

